{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d7ab","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9ec-c2bb-7943-8be0-a404f5b08a54"},"sequence":2608,"recorded_at":1780531400005211,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eeaf8872-3b6a-4c54-9252-9d526f344e1b","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"eeaf8872-3b6a-4c54-9252-9d526f344e1b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eeaf8872-3b6a-4c54-9252-9d526f344e1b"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Revision 5 is ready for review — handed off to review with board status `to-review`.\n\nBoth residual rev4 defects are repaired at the production boundary. Unregister now re-checks the initiating-session authority after the final stopped inspection and enforces the same authority inside the installer before `config.sh remove` begins, keeping the installer-wide lease and retry epilogue. Load/Apply use a per-editor operation generation: only the newest operation publishes or releases the busy state, session invalidation publishes an explicit retry message instead of wedging, and stale completions stay silent.\n\nEvidence: both exact rev4 probes adopted (red with 4 issues before, green after), 3 new tests (installer-boundary refusal + retry, latched same-Flow overlap through the real reducer, same-Flow retry in the new session), 4 silence-contract tests updated to the explicit-cleanup contract, and 3 narrowing mutants killed with retained-gate controls passing in each run — zero survivors. Full suites green (229 Swift + 62 Python, exit 0), fresh signed 1.2.0 candidate verified (TeamIdentifier 262RZ595FP), production runners untouched, candidate left uncommitted. Outcome artifact `TASK-260916-304bw2_catalog-lifecycle-r5-outcome.md` is attached on the board.","reason":null}}
